+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage with browser-local receipt and gift voucher signing.
+
+## Signing and verification
+
+The browser generates an ECDSA P-256 key pair through Web Crypto. The private key is nonextractable and stored as a CryptoKey in IndexedDB. Documents use SHA-256 and a recursively sorted JSON serialization to sign the envelope, including the algorithm, key fingerprint, and complete payload.
+
+Signed JSON downloads can be verified on the same browser. To verify on another device, first export the public key in **Your keys**, independently confirm its SHA-256 fingerprint through a trusted channel, and import it on the receiving device. A document's key identifier alone is never treated as trusted. Imported public keys persist in IndexedDB.
+
+This is a local signing identity, not an authenticated merchant issuance system. A signature proves integrity and a relationship to the trusted key; it does not prove payment, establish the signer as Daily Grind, or prevent duplicate voucher redemption. Official merchant issuance would require a provisioned merchant trust anchor and access-controlled signing and redemption services. Classical ECDSA is used; this implementation does not claim quantum resistance.
+
+Web Crypto needs a secure context (HTTPS or localhost) and IndexedDB access. Clearing browser data removes the signing key. There is intentionally no private-key export. Retain public keys to verify earlier documents. Fonts and the stock coffee photo load from Google Fonts and Unsplash; document content and keys are not uploaded by the application.
+
+## Automated checks
+
+Run `npm test`. Tests use Node's Web Crypto implementation for receipt/voucher round trips, public-key export/import, tampering rejection, unknown-key rejection, invalid envelopes, canonical ordering, and private-key nonextractability.
+
+No build step or runtime dependencies are required. Serve the static files using an HTTPS-capable static host.
